">Advanced</a> <span class=\"fn\">rest</span> <span class=\"fn\">it</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">τ</span> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">done</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Steps `it` past any `skip` steps. Calls `yield` with the next token and the iterator after it, or\n`done` at the end of the input. Written in continuation-passing style, and inlined, so that\nspecialization avoids allocating an intermediate result. Further `skip` steps go through a loop that\nreturns data rather than taking `yield`: a continuation passed into that loop would become a closure,\nallocated for every token even when nothing skips.","docLink":"./UnicodeFormat/Iterator/Basic.html#Unicode.nextToken","kind":"def","line":73,"name":"Unicode.nextToken","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-unicode-format/blob/929442f07486b2652bf358c2afa06a276eaab7cd/UnicodeFormat/Iterator/Basic.lean#L73-L89"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./UnicodeFormat/Iterator/Basic.html#Unicode.Advanced.of_skip\"><span class=\"name\">Unicode</span>.<span class=\"name\">Advanced</span>.<span class=\"name\">of_skip</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">ι </span><span class=\"fn\">τ</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Iterators/Basic.html#Std.Iterator\">Std.Iterator</a> <span class=\"fn\">ι</span> <a href=\"./Init/Control/Id.html#Id\">Id</a> <span class=\"f